            <ArticleTitle>Pathophysiologic substrate for ventricular tachycardia in coronary artery disease and non-ischemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>875-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sustained uniform monomorphic ventricular tachycardia is usually due to abnormalities of conduction, including coronary artery disease and right ventricular dysplasia. These conduction abnormalities are due to non-uniform anisotropy which is characterized by fragmented electrograms. Less is known about the pathophysiologic substrate of sustained ventricular tachycardia in the absence of coronary artery disease or cardiomyopathy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
